Here's a simple JavaScript function that accepts text and posts a message via the Slack API to the specified channel:

```javascript
function postToSlack(text, channel) {
  const webhookUrl = `https://hooks.slack.com/services/${process.env.SLACK_APP_ID}/${process.env.SLACK_APP_TOKEN}/${channel}`;
  fetch(webhookUrl, {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: {
      'Content-Type': 'application/json'
    },
    body: JSON.stringify({
      text
    })
  });
}
```

Make sure to replace `process.env.SLACK_APP_ID` and `process.env.SLACK_APP_TOKEN` with your actual Slack app ID and token. You can get these values from the Slack Developer Portal.

Also, make sure to install the `fetch` polyfill if you're using an older browser that doesn't support the `fetch` API. You can do this by adding the following line at the beginning of your script:

```javascript
import 'whatwg-fetch';
```

Now you can use the `postToSlack` function like this:

```javascript
postToSlack('Hello, world!', '#general');
```

This will post the message "Hello, world!" to the #general channel in Slack.

