double clothesPrice = 100;
double bookPrice = 20;

double totalCost = CalculateTotalCost(carPrice, clothesPrice, bookPrice);

Console.WriteLine("The total cost of the purchase is: " + totalCost);
```

This will output the total cost of the purchase, which should be $5200 (3000 + 100 + 20).

Yes, you can determine whether a message in Slack has been read or not using the Slack API. When you retrieve a message using the `chat.messages.get` endpoint, the API response includes a `read` field that indicates whether the message has been read.

The `read` field is set to `true` if the message has been read and `false` if it hasn't. You can use this field to filter messages that have been read or unread as needed.

Here's an example of how you might use the `chat.messages.get` endpoint to retrieve messages and filter out those that have been read:
```javascript
const slack = require('slack');

const token = 'your-slack-token';
const channel = '#general';

async function fetchMessages() {
  const client = new slack.Client(token);

  try {
    const responses = await client.chat.messages.get({
      channel,
      limit: 100, // Limit the number of messages retrieved
    });

    const messages = responses.map(response => response.messages);

    // Filter out read messages
    const unreadMessages = messages.filter(message => !message.read);

    console.log('Unread messages:', unreadMessages);
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Error fetching messages:', error);
  } finally {
    client.close();
  }
}

fetchMessages();
```
This code fetches up to 100 messages from the specified channel and filters out any messages that have been read. The remaining messages are logged to the console.

