To accomplish this task using the Accord.NET library in C#, follow these steps:

1. Install the Accord.NET NuGet package if you haven't already.
2. Create a new C# console application and add the following `using` statements at the top of your `Program.cs` file:
```csharp
using System;
using System.Collections.Generic;
using System.IO;
using System.Linq;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading.Tasks;
using Accord.MachineLearning.Classification;
using Accord.MachineLearning.Vectorization;
using Accord.Math;
```
3. Load the dataset of labeled sentences from a file (e.g., `dataset.csv`) into a list of `LabeledSample` objects:
```csharp
private static List<LabeledSample> LoadDataset(string filePath)
{
    var samples = new List<LabeledSample>();
    using (var reader = new StreamReader(filePath))
    {
        string line;
        while ((line = reader.ReadLine()) != null)
        {
            var parts = line.Split(',');
            var label = int.Parse(parts[0]);
            var text = parts[1];
            samples.Add(new LabeledSample(label, text));
        }
    }
    return samples;
}
```
4. Preprocess the dataset by tokenizing the text and converting it into a matrix of word counts:
```csharp
private static Matrix PreprocessDataset(List<LabeledSample> samples)
{
    var vectorizer = new CountVectorizer();
    var documents = samples.Select(s => s.Text).ToArray();
    var documentMatrix = vectorizer.Transform(documents);
    return documentMatrix;
}
```
5. Train the Naive Bayes classifier on the preprocessed dataset:
```csharp
private static NaiveBayesTrainer TrainNaiveBayes(Matrix documentMatrix, List<int> labels)
{
    var trainer = new NaiveBayesTrainer(documentMatrix, labels);
    return trainer.Train();
}
```
