To create a socket for chatroom using your given database structure, you'll need to follow these steps:

1. Create a PHP script that will handle the socket connection and communication.
2. Use a library like PHP-Socket or Ratchet to simplify the socket implementation.
3. Connect to the MySQL database to retrieve and store chat messages.

Here's an example of how you can create a socket for chatroom using PHP-Socket:

```php
<?php
require_once 'PHP-Socket/socket.php';
require_once 'config.php'; // Replace with your actual configuration file

// Set up the socket server
$server = new SocketServer('0.0.0.0', 8080);
$server->setHandler(function ($socket) use ($server) {
    // Handle incoming connections
    $socket->on('connection', function ($client) use ($server) {
        echo "New client connected\n";

        // Send a welcome message to the client
        $client->send("Welcome to the chatroom!\n");

        // Add the client to the list of connected clients
        $server->clients[] = $client;

        // Handle incoming messages from the client
        $client->on('message', function ($message) use ($client, $server) {
            // Broadcast the message to all connected clients
            foreach ($server->clients as $client) {
                $client->send($message);
            }
        });

        // Handle disconnections from the client
        $client->on('close', function () use ($server) {
            echo "Client disconnected\n";

            // Remove the client from the list of connected clients
            unset($server->clients[array_search($client, $server->clients)]);
        });
    });
});

// Start the socket server
$server->start();

// Connect to the MySQL database
$db = new mysqli($db_host, $db_user, $db_pass, $db_name);

// Check for any errors connecting to the database
if ($db->connect_error) {
    die("Error connecting to database: " . $db->connect_error);
}

